    "body": "## Parent\n\n#172\n\n## What to build\n\nDetect External Task Drift for Google-side title, notes, or due-date changes and Task Link Conflict for competing status changes, with every approved explicit resolution.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Google-side title, notes, or due-date changes never silently overwrite canonical content.\n- [ ] Content change places the link in changed-externally state with both projections available.\n- [ ] Restore app version pushes canonical content; Use external values deliberately updates the local Task; Remove link preserves both records.\n- [ ] Competing local and Google completion-state changes enter conflicted state and neither side wins implicitly.\n- [ ] Use app status, Use external status, and Remove link resolve completion conflict only after the selected operation succeeds.\n- [ ] The synchronization baseline is durable across restart.\n- [ ] `npm run check` is green.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #185 — Synchronize Google completion and missing-record state",
